   "text": "I read the structure in four pieces and assigned each stereocentre from the wedges and hashes using CIP priorities.\n\n**Left fragment.** This is a 7-hydroxy-5-methyl-6,7-dihydro-5H-cyclopenta[d]pyrimidine whose C4 carries a piperazine nitrogen. The drawing gives 5R (hashed methyl) and 7R (wedged OH), the same as the (5R,7R) pattern of ipatasertib.\n\n**Acyl piperazine and chlorophenyl centre.** The piperazine's other nitrogen is acylated by a C(=O)\u2013CH(4-chlorophenyl)\u2013CH2\u2013NH unit. The aryl group is on a wedge, and the CIP analysis gives S. The priorities are C(=O)N > CH2N > aryl.\n\n**Linker.** From the NH the chain is CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH. That is a PEG-type linker ending in an amide to the next fragment.\n\n**VHL ligand.**\n- The tert-leucine unit has S configuration (L), with the tert-butyl on a hash.\n- The 4-hydroxyproline is (2S,4R).\n- The proline carboxyl forms an amide with (S)-1-[4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)phenyl]ethylamine.\n\nI wrote the SMILES with the chirality tags worked out centre by centre. For the hydroxyproline and the benzylic amine I also checked the tags against the known SMILES of L-hydroxyproline and (S)-1-phenylethylamine.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H]1C[C@@H](O)c2ncnc(N3CCN(CC3)C(=O)[C@@H](c3ccc(Cl)cc3)CNCCOCCOCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N3C[C@H](O)C[C@H]3C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c3ccc(cc3)-c3scnc3C)c21"
